Voxel TERRAIN renderer (extender FUN_0000_9200 + its projection FUN_0000_8120) flat32 memory-model
reconstruction -- the oracle-proven cockpit terrain writer (docs/oracle_terrain_writer.md).

The opaque-LOD voxel ground renderer 9200 (op 0x09 -> 82c0 = 8120 projection -> 9200 texel walk ->
82d0 teardown) was decompiled but NEVER exercised in the port, so three flat32 base-losses were
latent.  All asm-verified vs re_out/fist_image.bin:

  * 8120 (0x8120): the per-heading SIN/COS projection table lives at image 0x9450 (asm 0x81af
    'lea ebx,[ebx*4+0x9450]'; reads [ebx]/[ebx+4]/[ebx+0x200]/[ebx+0x204]).  Ghidra base-lost two
    reads (&FUN_0000_944b -> a HOST function pointer; bare 0x9454 -> a host address) and 4x-over-
    scaled the other two (&DAT_0000_9650 + iVar4 with iVar4 already = idx*4).  All four rebuilt as
    byte arithmetic on g_mem+fist_ext_base.
  * 9200 (0x9200) horizon table: DAT_0000_9114 holds a FLAT image offset (8deb: (&PTR_748c)[detail]
    = 0x7568 for detail 1, the byte sky-skip table baked in the image; skip[0]=6 matches the oracle
    first-column ground truth).  The per-column read must be module-base-relative.
  * 9200 colormap sampler: SELF-MODIFYING code (stub 91e5 patches DAT_0000_3918 = the colormap base
    into the 'mov al,[eax+disp]' displacement at run time); Ghidra baked the pre-patch literal
    0x7fffffff.  DAT_0000_3918 is a Route-1 host pointer to the loaded colormap -> colormap[texcoord].

Extender-side, driven only by the FIST_R3D2 diagnostic seam (default OFF) -> behaviour-neutral for
the default boot + all verify flows (engine fist.c untouched).
